# @scalekit-sdk/node v2.6.2 — Complete API Reference

## 1. Main Exported Class & Constructor

**Exported as**: `ScalekitClient` (default export, also as named export and alias `Scalekit`)

```typescript
import { ScalekitClient } from '@scalekit-sdk/node';
// or
import Scalekit from '@scalekit-sdk/node';

class ScalekitClient {
  constructor(envUrl: string, clientId: string, clientSecret: string)

  // Sub-clients
  readonly organization: OrganizationClient;
  readonly connection: ConnectionClient;
  readonly domain: DomainClient;
  readonly directory: DirectoryClient;
  readonly passwordless: PasswordlessClient;
  readonly user: UserClient;
  readonly session: SessionClient;
  readonly role: RoleClient;
  readonly permission: PermissionClient;
  readonly auth: AuthClient;
  readonly webauthn: WebAuthnClient;
  readonly token: TokenClient;
  readonly m2m: M2MClient;
  readonly tools: ToolsClient;
  readonly connectedAccounts: ConnectedAccountsClient;
  readonly actions: ActionsClient;
}
```

---

## 2. `getAuthorizationUrl` — Build the Authorization URL

```typescript
getAuthorizationUrl(redirectUri: string, options?: AuthorizationUrlOptions): string
```

**Parameters:**

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `redirectUri` | `string` | Yes | URL where users are redirected after auth |
| `options` | `AuthorizationUrlOptions` | No | Optional config |

**`AuthorizationUrlOptions`:**
```typescript
type AuthorizationUrlOptions = {
  connectionId?: string;       // Specific SSO connection ID
  organizationId?: string;     // Organization ID to authenticate against
  scopes?: string[];           // Default: ['openid', 'profile', 'email']
  state?: string;              // CSRF protection state param
  nonce?: string;              // ID Token nonce
  domainHint?: string;         // Domain hint for org's IdP
  loginHint?: string;          // Email/login hint
  codeChallenge?: string;      // PKCE code challenge
  codeChallengeMethod?: string;// PKCE method (only 'S256' supported)
  provider?: string;           // Social provider: 'google', 'github', 'microsoft'
  prompt?: string;             // 'login', 'consent', 'create'
};
```

**Returns:** `string` — the full authorization URL (synchronous, no network call).

---

## 3. `authenticateWithCode` — Exchange Authorization Code

```typescript
authenticateWithCode(
  code: string,
  redirectUri: string,
  options?: AuthenticationOptions
): Promise<AuthenticationResponse>
```

**Parameters:**

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `code` | `string` | Yes | Authorization code from callback |
| `redirectUri` | `string` | Yes | Must match the one used in `getAuthorizationUrl` |
| `options` | `AuthenticationOptions` | No | PKCE verifier |

**`AuthenticationOptions`:**
```typescript
type AuthenticationOptions = {
  codeVerifier?: string;  // Required if PKCE was used
};
```

**`AuthenticationResponse`:**
```typescript
type AuthenticationResponse = {
  user: User;
  idToken: string;        // JWT ID token
  accessToken: string;     // Access token for API auth
  expiresIn: number;       // Token expiration in seconds
  refreshToken: string;   // Refresh token for token rotation
};
```

**`User` type:**
```typescript
type User = {
  id: string;
  username: string | undefined;
  name: string;
  givenName: string;
  familyName: string | undefined;
  email: string;
  emailVerified: boolean;
  phoneNumber: string | undefined;
  phoneNumberVerified: boolean | undefined;
  profile: string | undefined;
  picture: string | undefined;
  gender: string | undefined;
  birthDate: string | undefined;
  zoneInfo: string | undefined;
  locale: string | undefined;
  updatedAt: string | undefined;
  identities: Identity[];
  metadata: string | undefined;
};

type Identity = {
  connectionId: string;
  organizationId: string;
  connectionType: string;
  providerName: string;
  social: boolean;
  providerRawAttributes: string;
};
```

**Note:** The `User` object is constructed from the ID token's JWT claims. The raw token response also has `access_token`, `id_token`, `expires_in`, and `refresh_token` (see `TokenResponse` type).

---

## 4. `getLogoutUrl` — Generate Logout URL

```typescript
getLogoutUrl(options?: LogoutUrlOptions): string
```

**`LogoutUrlOptions`:**
```typescript
interface LogoutUrlOptions {
  idTokenHint?: string;            // ID Token previously issued to client
  postLogoutRedirectUri?: string;  // URL to redirect after logout
  state?: string;                  // Opaque state param for callback
}
```

**Returns:** `string` — the full logout URL (synchronous, no network call). The URL is constructed as `{envUrl}/oidc/logout?{qs}`.

**Example:**
```typescript
const logoutUrl = scalekitClient.getLogoutUrl({
  idTokenHint: idToken,           // optional
  postLogoutRedirectUri: 'https://example.com',
  state: 'some-state'
});
```

---

## 5. AgentKit / Tool-Related Methods

The SDK exposes two sub-clients for tool/agent functionality: `scalekitClient.tools` (ToolsClient) and `scalekitClient.actions` (ActionsClient).

### 5a. `ToolsClient` — `scalekitClient.tools`

#### `listTools`
```typescript
listTools(options?: {
  filter?: MessageInitShape<typeof FilterSchema>;  // see Filter type below
  pageSize?: number;
  pageToken?: string;
}): Promise<ListToolsResponse>
```

**`Filter` type** (from protobuf):
```typescript
type Filter = {
  summary?: boolean;
  provider: string;
  identifier: string;
  toolName: string[];          // repeated
  query?: string;               // text search across tool metadata
  connector?: string;
  organizationId?: string;
  userId?: string;
  connectedAccountId?: string;
};
```

**`ListToolsResponse` type:**
```typescript
type ListToolsResponse = {
  nextPageToken: string;
  totalSize: number;
  prevPageToken: string;
  toolNames: string[];
  tools: Tool[];
};
```

#### `listScopedTools`
```typescript
listScopedTools(
  identifier: string,
  options: {
    filter: MessageInitShape<typeof ScopedToolFilterSchema>;  // REQUIRED
    pageSize?: number;
    pageToken?: string;
  }
): Promise<ListScopedToolsResponse>
```

**`ScopedToolFilter` type:**
```typescript
type ScopedToolFilter = {
  providers: string[];       // repeated
  toolNames: string[];       // repeated
  connectionNames: string[]; // repeated
};
```

**`ListScopedToolsResponse` type:**
```typescript
type ListScopedToolsResponse = {
  nextPageToken: string;
  totalSize: number;
  prevPageToken: string;
  tools: ScopedTool[];
};
```

**`ScopedTool` type:**
```typescript
type ScopedTool = {
  tool?: Tool;
  identifier: string;
  connectedAccountId: string;
};
```

#### `listAvailableTools`
```typescript
listAvailableTools(
  identifier: string,
  options?: {
    pageSize?: number;
    pageToken?: string;
  }
): Promise<ListAvailableToolsResponse>
```

**`ListAvailableToolsResponse` type:**
```typescript
type ListAvailableToolsResponse = {
  nextPageToken: string;
  totalSize: number;
  prevPageToken: string;
  tools: Tool[];
};
```

#### `executeTool`
```typescript
executeTool(params: {
  toolName: string;              // REQUIRED
  identifier?: string;           // connected account identifier (email/workspace ID)
  params?: Record<string, unknown>;  // JSON params for the tool
  connectedAccountId?: string;  // direct CA ID (e.g., "ca_...")
  connector?: string;           // connector/provider name
  organizationId?: string;
  userId?: string;
}): Promise<ExecuteToolResponse>
```

### 5b. `ActionsClient` — `scalekitClient.actions`

The ActionsClient is a higher-level composition of ToolsClient + ConnectedAccountsClient, designed for agent workflows.

#### `actions.executeTool`
```typescript
executeTool(params: {
  toolName: string;              // REQUIRED
  toolInput: Record<string, unknown>;  // Note: called "toolInput" here, not "params"
  identifier?: string;
  connectedAccountId?: string;
  connector?: string;
  organizationId?: string;
  userId?: string;
}): Promise<ExecuteToolResponse>
```

**Note:** `ActionsClient.executeTool` maps `toolInput` → `params` when delegating to `ToolsClient.executeTool`. It also validates that `toolName` is non-empty.

#### `actions.getAuthorizationLink`
```typescript
getAuthorizationLink(params: {
  connectionName?: string;
  identifier?: string;
  connectedAccountId?: string;
  organizationId?: string;
  userId?: string;
  state?: string;
  userVerifyUrl?: string;
}): Promise<GetMagicLinkForConnectedAccountResponse>
```

**`GetMagicLinkForConnectedAccountResponse`:**
```typescript
type GetMagicLinkForConnectedAccountResponse = {
  link: string;       // The magic link URL
  expiry?: Timestamp; // Link expiry time
};
```

#### `actions.verifyConnectedAccountUser`
```typescript
verifyConnectedAccountUser(params: {
  authRequestId: string;
  identifier: string;
}): Promise<VerifyConnectedAccountUserResponse>
```

**`VerifyConnectedAccountUserResponse`:**
```typescript
type VerifyConnectedAccountUserResponse = {
  postUserVerifyRedirectUrl: string;
};
```

#### `actions.listConnectedAccounts`
```typescript
listConnectedAccounts(params?: {
  connectionName?: string;
  identifier?: string;
  provider?: string;
  organizationId?: string;
  userId?: string;
  pageSize?: number;
  pageToken?: string;
  query?: string;
}): Promise<ListConnectedAccountsResponse>
```

#### `actions.deleteConnectedAccount`
```typescript
deleteConnectedAccount(params: {
  connectionName?: string;       // Requires connectionName + identifier OR connectedAccountId
  identifier?: string;
  connectedAccountId?: string;
  organizationId?: string;
  userId?: string;
}): Promise<DeleteConnectedAccountResponse>
```

#### `actions.getConnectedAccount`
```typescript
getConnectedAccount(params: {
  connectionName?: string;       // Requires connectionName + identifier OR connectedAccountId
  identifier?: string;
  connectedAccountId?: string;
  organizationId?: string;
